&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;ProPublica&lt;/strong&gt; is an independent, nonprofit newsroom that produces investigative journalism in the public interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;While the vast majority of ProPublica’s work comes from our staff, we occasionally consider supporting ambitious accountability stories or projects from independent journalists whose ideas align with the mission of our organization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Here’s what journalists submitting proposals should know.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re open to investigations that are revelatory or substantially advance what is known on a subject of importance. The investigation should have the potential to trigger needed reforms by identifying a problem, who’s responsible and what should change. It should also clearly show harm. The investigation can be rooted in a place or focus on a person, but it should illuminate an issue of broader relevance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The best proposals have a clear hypothesis, typically based on significant reporting: They don’t wonder whether something bad is happening, they know it. Please include not only a general description of the topic, but also a sense of the anecdotes/data/documents you have gathered, what you expect to find and possible accountability stories you want to tell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, applicants should detail, as much as is possible at the outset, what an investigation will require: data work, travel, obtaining public records. It’s also important for us to know what data, documents and/or source relationships the reporter already has. Finally, we’d like to hear a bit about why you are particularly suited to do this investigation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We will begin reviewing applications as we receive them, and aim to notify candidates regarding your proposals within two weeks of submission.&amp;nbsp;Questions? Send an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:%20talent@propublica.org&quot;&gt;talent@propublica.org&lt;/a&gt;. No phone calls, please.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For those proposals we accept, we pay competitive freelance rates, including reporting expenses. Freelancers are independent contractors and will not be treated by ProPublica as employees for any purpose.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Independent contractors are responsible for paying any required taxes on any compensation received and for understanding the applicable tax laws. We will begin reviewing applications as we receive them, and aim to notify candidates regarding your proposals within two weeks of submission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We know there are great candidates who may not fit into what we’ve described above or who have important skills we haven’t thought of. If that’s you, don’t hesitate to apply and tell us about yourself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age or any other status protected under applicable law. We are dedicated to building an inclusive newsroom and encourage people from all backgrounds to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;ProPublica&lt;/strong&gt; is an independent, nonprofit newsroom that produces investigative journalism in the public interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Local Reporting Network aims to be responsive to the needs of local journalists. There are multiple ways of working with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The majority of our partnerships are yearlong accountability journalism projects of importance to local communities. We are taking on​ two more projects in 2026 and are recruiting for those right now. We will also be accepting 15 new projects in 2027.&lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/propublica/jobs/4617572006?gh_src=2b92d9bf6us&quot;&gt; &lt;/a&gt;We will reimburse a news organization for the salary of the selected reporter (up to $80,000 for 2026 and $82,500 for 2027, plus a benefits stipend). These will be selected on a rolling basis, with specific deadlines for each round.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Here are the details:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Winter 2026 opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Application deadline: Rolling, letters of interest to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:local.reporting@propublica.org&quot;&gt;local.reporting@propublica.org&lt;/a&gt; by Oct. 15, 2026.&lt;br&gt;Open to: Newsrooms in the states listed as eligible through our 50 State Initiative. Fellowship dates: Flexible, to start on or before Jan. 1, 2027.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spring 2027 cohort&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Application deadline: Rolling, no later than Jan. 25, 2027, by 11:59 p.m. ET. &lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/propublica/jobs/4617572006?gh_src=2b92d9bf6us&quot;&gt;Apply here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Open to: All applicants from English-language local and regional newsrooms in the United States and its territories. &lt;br&gt;Fellowship dates: April 1, 2027, through March 31, 2028.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summer 2027 cohort&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Application deadline: Rolling, no later than April 26, 2027, at 11:59 p.m. ET. &lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/propublica/jobs/4617572006?gh_src=2b92d9bf6us&quot;&gt;Apply here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Open to: Newsrooms in the states listed as eligible through our 50 State Initiative.&lt;br&gt;Fellowships dates: July 1, 2027, through June 30, 2028.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fall cohort&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Application deadline: Rolling, no later than July 26, 2027, at 11:59 p.m. ET.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/propublica/jobs/4617572006?gh_src=2b92d9bf6us&quot;&gt;Apply here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Open to: Newsrooms in the remaining states listed as eligible through our 50 State Initiative.&lt;br&gt;Fellowship dates: Oct. 1, 2027, through Sept. 30, 2028.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sarah Blustain&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assistant Managing Editor/Local&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ProPublica&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:local.reporting@ProPublica.org&quot;&gt;local.reporting@ProPublica.org&lt;/a&gt; (email)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We know there are great candidates who may not fit into what we’ve described above or who have important skills we haven’t thought of. If that’s you, don’t hesitate to apply and tell us about yourself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age or any other status protected under applicable law. We are dedicated to building an inclusive newsroom and encourage people from all backgrounds to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;ProPublica&lt;/strong&gt; is an independent, nonprofit newsroom that produces investigative journalism in the public interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;ProPublica is hiring a software engineer to work primarily on the systems and services that power our audience data platforms. This important role serves to advance ProPublica’s mission — publishing journalism with real-world impact — by enabling systems that bring us greater understanding of our audiences and donors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced engineer who believes in our mission and thrives in multifaceted roles, contributing both to the long-term product road map and to hands-on development. Your responsibilities will include shipping high-quality and resilient code and collaborating with designers, product managers, data analysts, other engineers and agency partners. You’ll write code, configure no- and low-code integrations, contribute to our documentation, share your expertise and proactively solve problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of our expanding, crossfunctional product team, you’ll work with colleagues across ProPublica’s engineering, audience and membership operations, ensuring that our capabilities align with our principles and advance our organizational objectives. This position reports to our director of product engineering and will work closely with the audience data and insights analyst.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and ship reader-facing features that drive membership — calls to action, donation flows, and account and authentication experiences — with clean, resilient code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate the systems behind them: messaging tools, payments and donation processing platforms, user accounts, CDP and CRM, and the data infrastructure that connect them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument the audience and donor journey. Set up accurate and actionable event tracking so every meaningful step is captured cleanly and becomes data we can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support making experimentation routine. Build the infrastructure for A/B testing and, with internal business teams, run experiments regularly so our decisions rest on evidence instead of guesswork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write front-end&amp;nbsp; services and integrations as needed. (Our site runs on Wordpress VIP.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with our engineering leaders, protect reader privacy and keep us compliant with legal and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years of experience in front-end software development and system integrations, with a track record of implementing and maintaining performant, secure, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interacting with audience and reader data platforms, such as Salesforce, Google Analytics, Parse.ly, Sailthru, or similar CRMs, CDPs and analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a customer data platform implementation within the last two years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and troubleshooting skills, with experience in a highly collaborative team environment, supporting diverse stakeholders and adapting solutions to evolving business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and effective spoken and written communication skills, with the ability to document technical processes and present complex integration workflows to both technical and nontechnical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel for occasional staff summits or other required events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience implementing solutions such as Piano or MonetizationOS or building similar functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Wordpress and/or Wordpress VIP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with at least one language used in web development, such as PHP, Typescript or vanilla JS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of doing hands-on work with cloud data warehouses like Google BigQuery and customer data platforms such as Braze or Hightouch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of newsroom workflows and a passion for journalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job is full time and includes &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.propublica.org/benefits/&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;. ProPublica is based in New York, but we’re open to remote candidates. We have offices in New York City; Washington, D.C.; Atlanta; Chicago; Phoenix; and Berkeley, California. Applicants must be eligible to work in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is subject to an in-office work requirement of two days per week in the New York City office. That requirement may be extended to other offices with 60 days’ notice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job is covered under the terms of a collective bargaining agreement with The NewsGuild of New York, Local 31003, CWA, AFL-CIO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this position is $120,000 to $145,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a good-faith estimate of what we expect to pay for this position. The final salary figure will take into account a person’s experience, accomplishment and location. ProPublica is committed to paying its staff equitably, and these ranges should not be considered career salary limits or caps.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will begin reviewing applications as we receive them, but we will continue to consider candidates as long as the posting remains live on our site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Send an email to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:%20talent@propublica.org&quot;&gt;talent@propublica.org&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No phone calls, please.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We know there are great candidates who may not fit into what we’ve described above or who have important skills we haven’t thought of. If that’s you, don’t hesitate to apply and tell us about yourself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age or any other status protected under applicable law. We are dedicated to building an inclusive newsroom and encourage people from all backgrounds to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;ProPublica&lt;/strong&gt; is an independent, nonprofit newsroom that produces investigative journalism in the public interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications will close on Monday, November 16th, 2026, at 11:59 p.m. ET.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In 2024, ProPublica launched a short-form vertical video team to adapt our long-form investigative journalism for audiences on Instagram, TikTok and YouTube Shorts. Since then, the team has amassed nearly 65 million views. Now we’re building out the second phase of our social video strategy and have &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.propublica.org/atpropublica/propublica-launches-youtube-team-and-expands-social-video-efforts&quot;&gt;launched a new YouTube team&lt;/a&gt; dedicated to producing midlength adaptations for the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a video editor and motion designer who has a passion for accountability journalism and is excited by the opportunity to bring our reporting to an increasing number of viewers who treat YouTube as a platform to learn about the world around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work alongside video producers on the YouTube team and will own the creative and technical postproduction for several assigned videos a month. As this is a new team, you will also be a key part of building the workflows and best practices that make our YouTube video pipeline sustainable as well as creating the visual identity that helps to answer: What should ProPublica look and sound like on YouTube?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The videos you help create for YouTube are meant to serve as standalone editorial products, and we’re looking for your platform-native expertise to drive experimentation that helps us learn quickly, adapt and deliver the most compelling storytelling formats while adhering to our rigorous editorial standards and practices. You should be comfortable working with reporters and editors across the newsroom as well as freelancers we’ll bring on to help with projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a temporary two-year role that will report to our director of multiplatform audience strategy. The YouTube team sits within the larger ProPublica audience team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with producers to create videos — and related promo cuts — that are grounded in ethical journalistic principles, standards and practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use editorial judgment to translate investigations and video scripts with the sensitivity, care and appropriate tone they require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the creative and technical postproduction for videos — editing, motion graphic design and animation, color grading and sound design — ensuring projects are shaped and paced for a YouTube-first audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end motion design workflows, including creating storyboards, animatics and the polished final products for videos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a central motion design library of MOGRTs, templates, toolkits and other reusable visual assets for teamwide use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ProPublica’s brand standards and overall design system, collaborating with the design and graphics teams, among others, to ensure visual cohesiveness in videos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate proactively with the team regarding project status and timelines and directly collaborate with producers on scoping and delivering videos on schedule.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple projects in various stages of production, sometimes meeting tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for candidates who have proven that they can use video editing and design skills for journalistic ends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have these skills and attributes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Four or more years of professional video editing and motion design experience in a newsroom, media organization or production studio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, with expert proficiency in both Adobe After Effects and Premiere Pro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that highlights videos you have edited specifically for YouTube, including hosted, vlog-style and/or explainer formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building tension in hooks, controlling pacing and navigating tonal shifts in video storytelling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are energized by the opportunity of being part of a founding team and creating something from scratch — establishing formats, defining visual languages and building efficient workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive while collaborating, seeking input from others and iterating your work based on feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And many of these:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience being part of a founding YouTube team or launching a new project initiative.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in on-site production, including shooting on professional camera equipment and knowledge of lighting and audio setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital asset management and video archival workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma and Google Workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job is full time and includes &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.propublica.org/benefits&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;. ProPublica is based in New York, but we’re open to remote candidates. We have offices in New York City; Washington, D.C.; Atlanta; Chicago; Phoenix; and Berkeley, California. Applicants must be eligible to work in the U.S. and have the ability to travel, as necessary, for team meetings, training and video-related duties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is subject to an in-office work requirement of two days per week in the New York City office. That requirement may be extended to other offices with 60 days’ notice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job is covered under the terms of a collective bargaining agreement with The NewsGuild of New York, Local 31003, CWA, AFL-CIO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this position is $90,000 to $115,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a good-faith estimate of what we expect to pay for this position. The final salary figure will take into account a person’s experience, accomplishment and location. ProPublica is committed to paying its staff equitably, and these ranges should not be considered career salary limits or caps.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will begin reviewing applications as we receive them, but we will continue to consider candidates as long as the posting remains live on our site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Send an email to talent@propublica.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No phone calls, please.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We know there are great candidates who may not fit into what we’ve described above or who have important skills we haven’t thought of. If that’s you, don’t hesitate to apply and tell us about yourself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age or any other status protected under applicable law. We are dedicated to building an inclusive newsroom and encourage people from all backgrounds to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
